{"ts": "2026-11-23T23:30:53.935201Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T2308Z-9bd2", "unit": "openspec:add-code-block-tools", "seq": 32, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "Checked in store.ts: submitLockedTx returns toRecord(row) when digest === row.approved_digest (line 349-351); approveSurface sets approved_by on the surface row and state approved with approved_digest = input.digest (lines 532-543); toRecord derives pendingDigest from the newest surface only when approved_by is null (line 196). So r4 after approved2 is an approved record with null pending, never deep-equal to r3 (drifted, approvedDigest D_WC, pendingDigest D_WC2) as the test asserts at line 140. The spec requires submitCodeBlocksTx to call submitAdapterSurfaceTx, so no production implementation can satisfy the assertion in place. The test plan's R4 (\"the same record, no new event\") and the spec's \"R4 changes nothing\" are satisfied by the idempotent pending resubmission the suggestion checks. Option 1 preserves the deepEqual and the later approval assertion; it is the correct fix, and the file is frozen, so only accept opens it.", "called": true, "tasks": ["2.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.24937025, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "71b33fb92bb86301cc269c3520c3c7bff7cd2f723ef5776e6ffdfd92c3581fc7", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/code/register.db.test.ts:129", "quote": "const approved2 = await approveSurface(db.appPool, a, \"snips\", { digest: `sha256:${D_WC2}`, selfApproval: true }, CAROL_USER, { clock: CLOCK });", "claim": "The test approves D_WC2 before the R4 resubmission block."}, {"ref": "src/tools/code/register.db.test.ts:140", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(r4, r3);", "claim": "The test asserts the post-approval resubmission equals the earlier drifted record r3."}, {"ref": "src/tools/code/register.db.test.ts:122", "quote": "assert.equal(rec3.state, \"drifted\");", "claim": "r3 is the drifted record with approvedDigest D_WC and pendingDigest D_WC2."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:349", "quote": "if (digest === row.approved_digest) {\n    return toRecord(tx, ctx, row);", "claim": "Resubmitting a digest equal to the approved digest returns the current (approved) row's record and writes nothing."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:538", "quote": "SET state = 'approved', approved_digest = $1", "claim": "approveSurface sets the server state to approved with the approved digest D_WC2, so the post-approval record differs from r3."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:196", "quote": "const pending = newest !== null && newest.approved_by === null ? newest : null;", "claim": "After approval the newest surface has approved_by set, so pendingDigest is null in r4 and not D_WC2 as in r3."}, {"ref": "src/tools/adapter-store.ts:57", "quote": "return submitLockedTx(", "claim": "submitAdapterSurfaceTx, which the spec requires submitCodeBlocksTx to call, delegates to submitLockedTx."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-code/spec.md#requirement-a-code-block-surface-fixes-the-trust-flags-and-is-registered-through-the-adapter-seam", "quote": "`submitCodeBlocksTx` SHALL call `submitAdapterSurfaceTx`", "claim": "No conforming implementation can bypass the seam's idempotent return, so the assertion in place is unsatisfiable."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-code/spec.md#scenario-a-server-registers-pending-a-changed-source-drifts-it-and-each-refusal-writes-nothing", "quote": "R4 changes nothing", "claim": "The spec's R4 is an idempotent resubmission that changes nothing, which the moved block checks while D_WC2 is pending."}, {"ref": "spec:test-plan.md#store-rows", "quote": "R4 `[WC2]` again: the same record, no new event.", "claim": "The test plan's R4 expects the same record and no new event, coherent only while D_WC2 is still pending."}]}
